INT. NEOSPORT ARENA - FINALS STAGE - NIGHT

Banks of LED. Ten thousand seats, a hush. Six chairs on a raised dais, six headsets. Stage lights low. Overhead, a countdown reads 00:04.

The match has been decided. Aftermath: the winners hold position, the losers don't.

HEAD REFEREE LIANG PETROV, 40s, headset and clipboard, stands at the bench with TECHNICAL DIRECTOR AMARA SOYINKA, 30s, laptop on a cart, and ADJUDICATOR FELIX BRANDT, 50s, steel-rimmed glasses and a rulebook.

CLOSE ON the main screen. The final frame freezes: a character mid-leap, a glitch rippling across its sprite.

PETROV
(into radio)
Hold the broadcast. All stations hold. Judges to the dais.

SOYINKA
(typing)
I've got packet loss on station four. Latency spiked at one-forty-two. That's not their connection. That's us.

BRANDT
Rule eleven point three. Interference by hardware fault voids the round if verified within sixty seconds. We are at fifty.

THE ARBITERS' PANEL, five officials in grey blazers, file up the steps as one, tablets raised, faces unreadable.

ANGLE ON station four. A competitor, a HOODIE PLAYER, lowers his hands from the keyboard and sits perfectly still, hood up, eyes down.

PETROV
Who's on four?

SOYINKA
Registered as Ghost_Rider. Real name's not on the sheet. He signed in under a handle.

BRANDT
(sharp)
Under a handle? That's a violation. Players must register legal names before qualifiers.

THE HOODIE PLAYER pulls back his hood. Late 20s, calm, a faint grin. DANTE VASQUEZ.

DANTE
(into mic, to the crowd)
Dante Vasquez. Since you asked.

Murmur. The ten thousand lean in. Soyinka turns her screen to Petrov. Brandt flips pages, Petrov unclips his radio, the panel exchanges glances, and the countdown ticks to zero.

SOYINKA
(quiet)
It's not a fault, Liang. It's a patch. Someone pushed a build during the round. The signature is his.

WE SEE Dante rise, step off the dais, and hand the referee a drive.

DANTE
It's all on there. Every match. Every edit. I wanted somebody to ask.

PETROV
(taking it, exhaling)
Right. Everybody sit down. We're going to do this by the book.
